course: dictionary
lesson: 15430
title: Startled and sudden surprise
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how a person or animal feels in one quick moment. «Startled» is one of them. Read the words around it: «The cat was startled by the loud bang and jumped off the sofa.» The loud bang came without warning, and the cat jumped. So startled must mean suddenly surprised.
explain: Startled is also the past form of the verb «startle», which means to surprise or frighten someone suddenly. «The bang startled the cat» means the bang made the cat jump. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence: «The cat was suddenly surprised by the loud bang» still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: Startled often describes a look or a movement. «She gave a startled look when the phone rang at midnight.» Her face showed a quick fright, not a slow worry. «Tom was startled out of his sleep by a clap of thunder» means he woke up suddenly with a jump.
explain: Animals that are startled may run away, kick or bite. That is why, near horses, dogs and wild animals, you should move slowly and quietly. Then you do not give them a sudden fright.
fact: Startled means suddenly surprised or a little frightened by something unexpected.
fact: Startled is the past form of the verb startle: «The noise startled the birds.»
fact: «Startled by» tells you what caused the surprise: «He was startled by the bang.»
fact: A «startled look» is a face that shows a quick surprise or fright.
fact: Startled animals may run, kick or bite, so move slowly and quietly near them.
exercise: «The cat was startled by the loud bang.» What does startled mean here? | Happy and playing | Hungry for food | Very sleepy and slow | *Suddenly surprised, so it jumped
exercise: In «The horse startled and ran across the field», what does startled tell you the horse felt? | *Suddenly frightened or surprised | Bored by the grass | Tired and hungry | Proud of winning the race
exercise: Why should you move slowly and quietly near a horse or a dog? | Because animals like loud noises | Because quiet people are easier to see | *Because a startled animal may run, kick or bite | Because fast movement helps them sleep
test: «Tom was startled out of his sleep by a clap of thunder.» What does startled out of mean? | *Woke suddenly with a jump | Sang a song in his sleep | Ran outside to play | Went to sleep very slowly
test: What does the verb «startle» mean? | To make something clean | To sing loudly | *To surprise or frighten someone suddenly | To sleep very deeply
exam: Which word could replace startled in «The dog was startled by the fireworks»? | *surprised | bored | sleepy | calm
